    {
     "type": "visual",
     "title": "Anatomy of a Breath",
     "content": "Before going deeper, here's the basic architecture every later lesson builds on. Air enters the nose or mouth, passes the pharynx and larynx, enters the trachea, and splits into bronchi feeding the lungs. The diaphragm — a dome-shaped muscle — does roughly 80% of the work of healthy breathing.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Anatomy of a Breath</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The pathway from nose to alveoli</text><ellipse cx=\"450\" cy=\"220\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"225\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nose</text><text x=\"620\" y=\"225\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"start\">- filters, warms, humidifies</text><ellipse cx=\"450\" cy=\"320\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"325\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pharynx</text><text x=\"620\" y=\"325\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"start\">- shared food / air corridor</text><ellipse cx=\"450\" cy=\"400\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"25\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"405\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Larynx</text><text x=\"620\" y=\"405\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"start\">- vocal cords; sound</text><rect x=\"430\" y=\"430\" width=\"40\" height=\"120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"500\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Trachea</text><text x=\"620\" y=\"495\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"start\">- windpipe; rings of cartilage</text><line x1=\"450\" y1=\"550\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"650\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"450\" y1=\"550\" x2=\"530\" y2=\"650\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"350\" y=\"680\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L bronchus</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"680\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R bronchus</text><ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"780\" rx=\"100\" ry=\"120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"580\" cy=\"780\" rx=\"100\" ry=\"120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"790\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lungs</text><text x=\"450\" y=\"825\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">~480 million alveoli</text><path d=\"M 200 920 Q 450 880 700 920\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"965\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Diaphragm</text><text x=\"450\" y=\"1000\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">~80% of healthy breathing work</text><text x=\"450\" y=\"1050\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Surface area of alveoli ~ a tennis court.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Every breath travels this pathway — but most of the work happens at the diaphragm."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Pulmonauts: Nestor's Cast",
     "content": "Nestor calls the underground network of breathing researchers 'pulmonauts.' Carl Stough rehabilitated emphysema patients with breath retraining. Patrick McKeown carried the Buteyko method west. Wim Hof popularized cold-and-breath. Mike Mew turned orthodontics into airway development. Each thread of the book follows one or more of these figures.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Pulmonauts</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nestor's cast of breathing pioneers</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"190\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"230\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">Carl Stough</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"265\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">1926-2000 - Choral conductor turned breath therapist</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"300\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\">Worked with emphysema patients, Olympic athletes; retrained diaphragm</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"350\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"390\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">Patrick McKeown</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"425\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">Asthmatic Irish researcher</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"460\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\">Brought Soviet Buteyko method west; \"The Oxygen Advantage\"</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"510\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"550\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wim Hof</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"585\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">\"The Iceman\" - Dutch extreme athlete</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"620\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\">Tummo-derived hyperventilation + cold exposure; immune modulation</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"670\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"710\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">John & Mike Mew</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"745\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">British orthodontists / orthotropists</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"780\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\">Argue jaw shape is malleable; tongue posture builds airways</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"830\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"870\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">Anders Olsson</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"905\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">Swedish breath coach, Nestor's nasal-phase partner</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"940\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\">Slow breathing protocols; CO2 tolerance training</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1040\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Outsiders. Self-experimenters. Rejected by mainstream — then validated.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Nestor's heroes are mostly outsiders who rebuilt breathing science from scratch."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "In Nestor's Stanford experiment, what happened to his blood pressure during the 10-day mouth-breathing phase?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "It dropped significantly due to better oxygenation",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "It rose by about 13 points",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "It stayed identical to baseline",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "It rose only during exercise, not at rest",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Nestor's BP rose about 13 points during the mouth-breathing phase and normalized within days of returning to nasal breathing — one of the most striking measurements of the experiment.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Quiz: Stanford BP</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mouth-only phase, 10 days</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"900\" x2=\"900\" y2=\"900\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"300\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"900\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"305\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\">140</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"605\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\">120</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"905\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\">100</text><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"700\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#10b981\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"690\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#10b981\"/><circle cx=\"410\" cy=\"680\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#10b981\"/><circle cx=\"490\" cy=\"600\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/><circle cx=\"570\" cy=\"500\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/><circle cx=\"650\" cy=\"400\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/><circle cx=\"730\" cy=\"380\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/><circle cx=\"810\" cy=\"700\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#10b981\"/><polyline points=\"250,700 330,690 410,680 490,600 570,500 650,400 730,380 810,700\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"350\" y=\"980\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nasal baseline</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"980\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mouth-only</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"980\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Recovery</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"200\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BP rose ~13 points during mouth-only phase</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Nestor's own data: airway choice moved blood pressure substantially."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "What breath rate did Italian researchers (Bernardi et al.) find independently encoded in both the Catholic rosary's Ave Maria and yoga's mantra?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "About 12 breaths per minute (typical resting rate)",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "About 5.5 breaths per minute",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "About 20 breaths per minute (mild exertion)",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "About 2 breaths per minute (advanced pranayama only)",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Bernardi's 2001 BMJ study showed both the Ave Maria recited in Latin and the Sanskrit 'om mani padme hum' mantra paced breathing to about 5.5 breaths per minute — the resonant frequency of the cardiovascular system.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Quiz: The Resonant Rate</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bernardi, BMJ, 2001</text><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"550\" r=\"280\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"540\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"80\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5.5</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">breaths / minute</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ave Maria (Latin): ~5.5 bpm</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"940\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Om Mani Padme Hum: ~5.5 bpm</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"990\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Maximum HRV occurs near this rate</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Two religions, one number — the body's resonant breath."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Book's Big Claims",
     "content": "By the end of Breath, Nestor argues that proper breathing can lower blood pressure, end chronic snoring, improve athletic performance, ease anxiety, modulate immune function, and even reshape the face. Some claims are well-established in physiology; others are emerging. This course covers each in evidence-graded depth.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nestor's Big Claims</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evidence strength varies — we'll grade each</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"190\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"225\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">STRONG</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"255\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">Nasal breathing produces nitric oxide and humidifies air</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"290\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"325\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">STRONG</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"355\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">Slow breathing improves HRV and lowers BP short-term</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"390\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"425\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">STRONG</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"455\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">Mouth breathing predicts OSA, dry mouth, decay</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"490\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"525\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">MODERATE</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"555\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">Buteyko helps asthmatics reduce medication use</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"590\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"625\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">MODERATE</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"655\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">Wim Hof method modulates short-term immune response</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"690\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"725\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">EMERGING</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"755\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">Tongue posture reshapes adult faces (controversial)</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"790\" width=\"940\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"825\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\">EMERGING</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"855\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\">\"Lung capacity is largest predictor of lifespan\" (Framingham)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"970\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Read Nestor as a journalist marshaling evidence,</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1005\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">not a textbook — we'll separate signal from enthusiasm.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "We'll grade each claim as we go: strong, moderate, or emerging."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice 1: Notice Your Default Breath",
     "content": "Before changing anything, observe. For the next 24 hours, do a 'breath check' three times: morning, after a meal, and during work stress. Each time, answer: (1) Is my mouth open or closed? (2) Am I breathing into my chest or belly? (3) Roughly how many breaths per minute? Write the numbers down. You are establishing your baseline — and the act of noticing alone often slows the breath.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Practice: Breath Check</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Three observations, 24 hours</text><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"350\" r=\"100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"345\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Morning</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"380\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">on waking</text><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"350\" r=\"100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"345\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Post-meal</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"380\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">~20 min after</text><circle cx=\"880\" cy=\"350\" r=\"100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"880\" y=\"345\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Stress</text><text x=\"880\" y=\"380\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">at work / driving</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"510\" width=\"800\" height=\"430\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"560\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Questions Each Time</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"630\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\">1. Mouth open or closed?</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"685\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\">2. Chest or belly rising?</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"740\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\">3. Count breaths for 60 seconds.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"795\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\">4. Nose blocked on one side?</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"850\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\">5. Sighing or holding breath?</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"905\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\">6. Tongue: roof of mouth or floor?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1000\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bring numbers to Lesson 2. No fixing yet — just see.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1040\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Most learners discover they breathe 18-20 bpm under stress.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Baseline first, intervention second — the cornerstone of any breath practice."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice 2: One Conscious Minute",
     "content": "Set a timer for exactly 60 seconds. Sit upright, close your mouth, and breathe only through your nose. Count each full breath cycle (in + out = 1). Do not try to slow down — just breathe normally with the mouth shut. Record the count. This is your 'resting nasal rate.' Repeat for three consecutive days and average. We'll use this number in Lesson 3.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Practice: 60-Second Count</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your resting nasal rate</text><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"450\" r=\"240\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"550\" y1=\"450\" x2=\"550\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"550\" y1=\"450\" x2=\"700\" y2=\"500\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"460\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"32\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">60</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"500\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">seconds</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"780\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Protocol</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"830\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Sit upright, shoulders relaxed</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"865\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Mouth closed, breathe nose-only</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Breathe normally — don't perform</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4. Count each in+out as ONE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1000\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Average of 3 days = your baseline rate.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1040\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Typical adult: 12-20. Trained: 6-10. Yogi: 3-5.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "A simple count establishes the number we'll work to lower."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "According to Nestor, why has 'how we breathe' been overlooked by modern medicine?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Because breathing is impossible to measure objectively",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Because no single specialty owns the integrated act of breathing",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Because pharmaceutical companies suppressed the research",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Because ancient texts were lost and never recovered",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Nestor's view is institutional, not conspiratorial: lungs go to pulmonology, noses to ENT, teeth to dentistry, anxiety to psychiatry — and breathing as an integrated act falls between the cracks of every specialty.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Quiz: A Gap in Medicine</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why was breath overlooked?</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"250\" width=\"700\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"295\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pulmonology</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">treats LUNGS</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"400\" width=\"700\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"445\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">ENT</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"485\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">treats NOSE</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"550\" width=\"700\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"595\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dentistry</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"635\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">treats JAW</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"700\" width=\"700\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Psychiatry</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"785\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">treats ANXIETY</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nobody treats the BREATH itself.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"970\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nestor's project is to stitch the act back together.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "An institutional gap, not a conspiracy."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quote",
     "title": "Nestor's Thesis",
     "content": "\"Of all the things we do as humans, the simplest is the most overlooked. We assume because we are alive that we are breathing well. We are not.\" Across the next seven lessons, we'll trace Nestor's evidence from nostril to alveolus to ancient monastery — and translate his findings into a daily practice you can actually use.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Thesis</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">From Nestor's introduction</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"280\" width=\"900\" height=\"380\" fill=\"#2a2a4e\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"4\" rx=\"20\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"370\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">\"Of all the things we do as humans,</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"410\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">the simplest is the most overlooked.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"490\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">We assume because we are alive</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"530\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">that we are breathing well.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"32\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-style=\"italic\">We are not.\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"650\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">- James Nestor</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"780\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Coming Up</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"830\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L2: Nose vs Mouth + nitric oxide</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"865\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L3: Slow breathing + HRV</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L4: CO2 tolerance + Buteyko</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L5: Mouth taping + sleep</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"970\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L6: Wim Hof + Tummo</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1005\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L7: Posture + face shape</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1040\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L8: Your daily protocol</text></svg>",
      "caption": "We end where Nestor begins — with the claim that we have forgotten how to breathe."
     }
    }
